  "summary": "A rotary vane compressor has a slotted rotor turning off-centre in a cylinder. Vanes slide out against the cylinder wall and divide the space into cells. On one side the cells grow and draw air in; on the other side they shrink and compress the air before it leaves through the discharge port. Oil injected into the cells seals and cools.",
